# Bounded wake resend for the DEPLOYED directory server (c2-connect-first-try r1, F3).
#
# Base: /opt/gnlink/remote60-directory/server.js as deployed,
#       sha256 27b730e7a3c89631fb37c10515f664c74c4412509c6d7170c8dcbd2ec20139d1
# After: sha256 9f54e188180c52b60c5a1063bc4b3988259dec91bdc9b7113175eb8e0815ede3
#
# Why: the wake is a burst of three datagrams inside 300ms. A host that misses all three --
# asleep, or with its heartbeat 25 seconds away -- is never poked again, and the capability sits
# in pendingPunch until it expires. The client's first click fails and its second works, which is
# the company PC1 -> PC2 complaint.
#
# What this adds: after the burst, one datagram a second, at most ten, stopping the moment the
# capability is handed to the host. Thirteen datagrams per connect in the worst case, ten seconds
# of them, inside the thirty seconds the capability lives anyway.
#
# Bounds, all re-checked on every tick rather than captured when the timer was armed:
#   - one timer per HOST, not per connect; a second connect replaces the first
#   - a global ceiling of 64 such timers
#   - WAKE_MIN_INTERVAL_MS (1s per host) still refuses a second datagram inside a second
#   - stops on: capability handed over, none left (expired), host gone, host stale, budget spent
#   - the target address is recomputed each tick, so a heartbeat that moves the host is followed
#
# One wording change, no behaviour: the [capability] collected line now ends with
# meaning=handed-to-response. That line has been read as if the host had acknowledged something.
# It has not -- the host sends nothing back for a capability. Appended, so the existing keys and
# their order are unchanged.
#
# The tick is wrapped in try/catch. It runs detached from any request, so an exception in it has
# nothing to catch it and would take the process down. Not hypothetical: the first cut of this
# change looked up hosts in a Map that is actually a plain object, and the server died.
#
# Nothing here listens to anything the host sends. The host answers punches now (C1), and those
# answers go to whoever punched it, never to this server -- so they cannot re-arm or extend any
# of this. Pinned by apps/directory/test/wake_resend_test.js.
#
